president biden is sending a stark  message to russia and vladimir putin  president biden is announcing the  deployment of more u.s troops to europe  the move is a declaration that russia is  a direct threat and it's part of the  biggest shift in nato defense priority  since the end of the cold war president  putin says his military will respond in  kind to any threats from nato countries  nancy cordes is at the nato summit in  madrid nancy good morning so what else  is nato doing to respond to russia's  invasion of ukraine  well that just for context right now  nato has a rapid response force of about  40 000 troops spread throughout the  continent under this new plan the number  of allied troops on high alert would  grow more than seven fold to 300 000  troops and the u.s would establish its  first permanent base  near the russian border in poland  the new military measures are a  recognition that russian aggression  could continue for some time the u.s  deployments will include two more navy  destroyers to spain two f-35 fighter jet  squadrons to the u.k and an additional  combat brigade to romania we're going to  make up sure that nato is ready to meet  threats from all directions across every  domain land air and the sea president  biden is expected to announce that the  u.s will also give ukraine a  medium-range air defense system known as  naysams  it's capable of shooting down the kind  of cruise missile russia used to strike  a busy shopping mall in central ukraine  earlier this week  but ukrainian president vladimir  zelinsky appearing remotely urged the  nato leaders here to do even more he  said he can't break russia's dominance  without more artillery tanks and armored  vehicles  we need weapon weapons  igor joka is zielinski's deputy chief of  staff what does victory look like for  ukraine what does winning the war mean  bringing back all the ukrainian  territories definitely no other  compromises are possible russian  president vladimir putin denounced  nato's military expansion and the formal  invitation for sweden and finland to  join the western alliance  if nato troops and infrastructure are  deployed to sweden and finland he warned  we will be compelled to create the same  threats to the territory that is now  creating threats for us  president biden is likely to get  questions about all of this at a press  conference he's holding here at the nato  summit this morning it is his final  formal engagement at the summit before  flying home to washington d.c gail  thank you very much nancy cordes  reporting from madrid
 

